{"name": "long-rambling-entry", "entry": {"id": 18, "entryType": "BUY", "body": "Long note because I want to remember why I did this. I've owned AMZN on and off for years and always sold too early. This time I sat down and actually went through the last eight quarters myself. Retail is noisy and I don't care much about it. What matters is AWS margins expanding again and the ads business, which is now huge and high margin. Those two together are most of the operating income. People keep talking about the stock being expensive but on those segments it isn't. I bought 15 shares today. I'm pretty confident, call it 4 out of 5. The plan is to hold for years and not touch it on every dip like last time. The one thing that would make me sell is AWS growth dropping below 10% for two quarters in a row, because then the whole story breaks. Otherwise I leave it alone and check in each quarter.", "ticker": "AMZN", "timestamp": "2026-03-03T15:30:00Z", "tags": []}, "expected": {"hasThesis": true, "hasExit": true, "horizon": "years", "conviction": 4, "ideaSource": "own_research", "emotions": ["confident"], "tickers": ["AMZN"], "reasoningBasis": "fundamentals", "thesisOutcome": null}}
